00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:53.020
A lot to cover in our time here together.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.500
Couple things I wanna talk about.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.358
First thing I wanna talk
about is the concept of

00:01:59.358 --> 00:02:04.358
guilting people by giving
so much without expectation

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:09.714
that it creates the outcome
that you're looking for.

00:02:09.714 --> 00:02:10.547
(clapping)

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:11.721
Thanks, Mom.

00:02:11.721 --> 00:02:14.840
(audience laughing)

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.140
And I think it's an interesting thing,

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.220
because when I come to talks,

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.020
I'm always trying to
provide the most value

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.240
that I possibly can,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.676
and I'm trying to find platforms
that connect all of us,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.880
everybody in here is in a
different place in their journey,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.340
whether it's entrepreneurship,

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.240
or working in environment, start up,

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.742
there's just so much different
shit happening in the room

00:02:32.742 --> 00:02:35.470
that it's hard when you speak

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.470
because you don't wanna talk so narrow

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.090
that half the audience is checked out

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.840
'cause there's zero relevance.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.500
And that's why I love
talking about attention

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.660
and I'll get to that in a minute

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.090
because the one thing I'm sure of

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.880
is that every single person
here needs to understand

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.410
that they have to grab attention

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.950
and then storytell and create
the action that they want.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:57.700
On the same token, it is that
action that fascinates me.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.430
Nobody's sitting here
without some sort of ambition

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.750
to create something to happen.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.970
And I think there's a real huge
mistake and misunderstanding

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.920
or what, to be very frank, what I think

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.950
has gotten me here versus
other people in other statures

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:14.870
and different opportunities,

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.030
and there's just a very big difference

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.850
between branding and selling.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.600
And I think for a lot of you in this room,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.790
there's a real interesting conversation

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.750
because you want something to happen

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.300
and either A you can sell,

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.600
I think you guys know
what selling looks like.

00:03:31.014 --> 00:03:34.014
(audience cheering)

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.310
Or you can brand and I'm
intrigued by branding

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:44.900
because branding's funny, right?

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.120
Branding, so many of you right now

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.930
are wearing clothes that you're wearing

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.320
not because Vans tagged you, right,

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.580
and cookied you or gave you
a special deal for one day,

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:02.010
it's because they built a
brand and you wanted to buy it,

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.750
and I would implore all of you,

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.170
and this is, for so many of you,

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:10.480
you have 10, 20, 30, 40,
50 years of your career

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.240
and you need to use that as leverage

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.810
because when you have time on your hands,

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:21.500
you can run a marathon instead of the 99%

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.860
of what I see everyday
which is everybody's

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.710
putting on their sprinting shoes

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:29.450
and trying to sell and close
on the first transaction,

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:32.270
which is just not an
effective longterm strategy.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.410
It has value, it works, I get it.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.660
I love selling stuff.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.030
I love selling my new K-Swiss sneakers,

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.675
I love selling wine, I love
selling books, I like it.

00:04:40.675 --> 00:04:43.870
But there's such a better way

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:45.460
if you're playing the long game.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:47.330
And I think it's about bringing value.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.640
The thing that I obsess about,

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.850
I mean I literally have
been reading, and I know,

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.480
'cause I see you guys see
me interacting with you,

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:57.550
I'm literally reading your
two tweets in the back room

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:01.080
and liking it, I'm engaging
and paying attention,

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.790
and trying to figure out how
am I going to bring value

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:07.890
to this specific audience,
this specific time,

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.690
in an environment where
I know a lot of you

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:12.220
have already watched plenty of my content.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:13.870
Like how the fuck do you figure that out?

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.570
And it's intriguing to me

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:19.150
that as I go down the path of success,

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:24.150
I'm trying harder to bring
value, not the other way around.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.310
And look, to me that is the framework.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:29.340
To me the framework is
legacy not currency.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:32.210
To me the framework is
doing the right thing

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.220
is always the right thing.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.060
To me the things that
are making the people

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.010
achieve going forward, and my friends,

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.450
why do you think all this stuff is

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.680
happening in Hollywood right now?

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.342
The truth is gonna be undefeated.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:46.080
The internet is now the middle man,

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:50.120
for retail, for media, for our society.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.320
That is the way it is now.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.800
The internet is the middle man,

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.130
which means nobody's in
control except for the

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.590
end audience at scale.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.410
You may sit here and dwell 'cause you're

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.260
a defensive minded person

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.470
and think somebody's controlling shit.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.370
Facebook's not controlling shit.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.210
Facebook's exposing you 'cause you're

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.763
the one liking that shit.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.837
So we sit around and we
dwell and we go on defense

00:06:15.837 --> 00:06:17.670
and we think and all this,

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:20.830
and what we need is
dramatic accountability.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.220
You know how many people
in this audience right now

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.460
say that they're passionate
about too many things

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:28.660
and that's why they haven't done anything?

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.690
That's a fucking excuse to not do.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.430
You're not too talented
in too many things,

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.144
you're fucking lazy.

00:06:36.144 --> 00:06:38.170
(audience laughing)

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:41.470
And so I'm really intrigued
by a lot that's going on.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:44.440
But the thing that I
know more than anything

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:49.060
is that we're living through
the single greatest era

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:52.460
for humans ever right now.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.100
I know that we're
deploying plenty of things

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.230
that we're upset about,

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:58.230
and there's a lot of tension in the air,

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:59.660
and I think that's appropriate.

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:02.550
I just don't think that we
put things into context.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.920
You may not be happy about certain things

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.910
and technology or politics
or business or what have you.

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:10.853
But that's a hell of a lot
better than the black plague.

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:14.255
And so to me.

00:07:14.255 --> 00:07:15.127
(audience laughing)

00:07:15.127 --> 00:07:16.008
It is.

00:07:16.008 --> 00:07:17.020
Like I know shit sucks sometimes.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.570
But remember Hitler?

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.419
(audience laughing)

00:07:21.419 --> 00:07:25.610
So I'm extremely optimistic.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:27.950
I'm extremely positive what's going on.

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:30.820
And it's all because of
the framework of this talk.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:31.663
This thing.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:36.290
You have to, how many people
do not have a cell phone?

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:37.163
Raise your hand.

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:39.500
Cool.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:42.220
Zero, by the way, for
everybody in the front rows.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:46.900
This thing is ridiculously powerful.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:51.020
This thing is the remote
control of our society.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:54.067
This thing has eliminated every excuse

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:55.830
out of your fucking mouth.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.680
Because if you have to work 9:00 to 6:00

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:01.400
to pay the bills, to pay
your dues, to pay your debts,

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.520
that is exactly right and appropriate,

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.590
everybody comes from
different starting points.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:08.620
I have unbelievable empathy to that.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:12.060
The exciting thing, though,
is that our grandparents

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.750
didn't have this thing.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.720
They had to work 9:00
to 6:00, 9:00 to 7:00,

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.650
and then there was only so much upside

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.960
that they could create
for themselves longterm,

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.840
from 7:00 to 2:00 in the morning.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.480
This thing has fundamentally
changed everything.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.890
And I just think we take it for granted.

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:28.830
I really wish everybody understood

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.950
the power that's literally
sitting in their hands right now.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:34.280
This is literally a media creation

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.720
and distribution tool that would have cost

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.610
tens of millions of dollars

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.140
if you understand distribution.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.770
The technology probably costs $20,000,

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:43.940
you know 25 years ago.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:45.781
Cameras, this, that, fine.

00:08:45.781 --> 00:08:48.140
The distribution?

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:51.470
You would have had to shoot
a satellite into space.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:53.950
You would have had to
buy a printing press.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.640
You would have had to buy trucks.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:57.330
You would have had to done so much.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.200
The fact that every person here

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.510
can literally turn this on themselves,

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:04.920
create content around something
they're interested in,

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.890
and then have platforms like

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:08.480
YouTube and Facebook and Instagram

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.420
and Twitter and LinkedIn distribute it,

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:14.890
let me remind you, at no cost,

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:19.870
is so batshit crazy for all
of us old fuckers in here,

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.780
that I just wish people would
not take it for granted.

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.435
And so my friends, I come here tonight

00:09:25.435 --> 00:09:28.160
to really try to pull off one move.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:32.160
Can I actually take somebody,
even if they're a huge fan,

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:34.210
or if they've never heard of me before,

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:38.520
and tweak their perspective
on what's actually going on?

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.710
Can I convince one of you that

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:44.890
nobody gives a shit about
your headaches and problems,

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.400
and when you complain,

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.620
you're just taking minutes off the board,

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.680
and energy off the board,
from doing something about it.

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:55.105
Literally I am fascinated by the

00:09:55.105 --> 00:09:57.260
inability to be held accountable.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.990
I am fascinated that you actually are

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.560
coming up and spending energy

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.150
and trying to say why
you're not successful

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:07.803
because you're older brother
did some shit in 1996.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:10.750
And so (laughing) sorry.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.190
I mean it's super interesting to me.

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:14.170
I read, and read, and read.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:17.310
I don't watch, outside of
watching New York Jets football,

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:18.420
and now the Knicks are starting

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:21.720
to maybe try to do something,
so a little Knicks basketball,

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:25.290
like I consume nothing but your comments.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:26.740
And I get into rabbit holes.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:28.430
You know how on Wikipedia or YouTube,

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:29.520
you start off watching something

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.970
and then three hours later you're watching

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:33.408
like penguins shitting on each other?

00:10:33.408 --> 00:10:34.530
(audience laughing)

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.820
That's what I do with comments.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.320
You guys leave comments.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:42.790
80% of it is either overwhelmingly like,

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:45.190
I'm the messiah, which
you can keep doing that.

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:46.023
It feels great.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:49.392
Or I'm a snake oil
salesman and piece of shit,

00:10:49.392 --> 00:10:51.210
I love that even more, by the way,

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.120
keep feeding me you fucking losers.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:57.680
But the 20%'s super interesting to me.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:59.300
Which is they'll say something,

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:02.300
and of that 20%, 10% say
something really intriguing.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.740
I'm a little bit of an enigma.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.620
I'm an interesting kind of character

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:08.662
in the way that I communicate
versus my actions.

00:11:08.662 --> 00:11:10.690
Actually watch this.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:11.523
How many people here.

00:11:11.523 --> 00:11:14.540
Honest, remember lying is the devil.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.130
How many people here honestly,

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:18.450
the first time or two
that they came across me,

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.270
thought I was a dick
face and didn't like me?

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:21.290
Raise your hands.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.123
Raise 'em high.

00:11:23.523 --> 00:11:24.940
Ooh, that's a little too many.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.290
(audience laughing)

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.510
And so knowing that truth,

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:33.010
I am always fascinated because
I'm able to judge people

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:34.550
on how they react to me.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:35.980
A lot of the people
that raised their hands

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:37.720
were in a mindset at the time

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.760
of not being comfortable being suffocated

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.410
from the excuse that
they were comfortable in.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.280
If you ask me when I look at my content

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:44.900
and take myself out of it,

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:48.110
the thing that I'm doing
is I'm putting pressure.

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:51.470
I'm putting pressure,
and I'm using the truth

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:54.510
as my pressure point, which
is making me successful

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:56.880
and why so many people benefit from me.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.280
Because once you can flip over

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.390
